---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
const lang = 'en';
---
<Layout
  title="Riding in Morocco on your own motorcycle · CDM Motorsport"
  description="Riding Morocco on your own motorcycle: shipping, paperwork, insurance and full CDM Motorsport support throughout your off-road motorcycle tour."
  ogImage="/img/gallery/gallery-13.jpg"
  lang={lang}
>
  <section class="phero short" style="background-image:url('/img/gallery/gallery-13.jpg')">
    <div class="wrap c">
      <div class="eyebrow" style="color:#e8c9a6">Practical</div>
      <h1>Your own <em>bike</em></h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pad">
    <div class="wrap article">
      <div class="meta reveal">Practical · 5 min read</div>
      <div class="big reveal" style="margin-bottom:24px">
        Riding in Morocco<br />on your own <em>motorcycle</em>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal">
        <p>
          Some riders really want to be on their own machine, the one they know inside out.
          I completely understand, and it's absolutely doable. You just need to plan the
          logistics a little in advance.
        </p>
        <p>
          To get the bike here, you have two options: road and ferry from Spain if you've
          got the time and the appetite for the trip, or a specialist shipping company that
          handles everything. Either way, allow for the lead times.
        </p>
        <p>
          On the paperwork side, don't cut corners: registration document, green card, a
          third-party insurance policy valid in Morocco, and above all a repatriation
          insurance that actually covers off-road riding. That's the kind of detail people
          forget and then get stuck with at the border.
        </p>
        <p>
          Once you're here, even on your own bike, you get the full support package: the
          4x4 following along, luggage transport, daily mechanical check-ups. You ride
          light, I handle the logistics.
          <a href="/en/option-4x4">The 4x4 and companions option</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          Riding your own motorcycle means keeping your feel and your reflexes on terrain
          that has nothing in common with home. My job is to make sure everything runs
          smoothly so all you have to do is enjoy it.
        </p>

        <p style="margin-top:28px">
          Got a question about your plans?
        </p>
        <a href="/en/reserver" class="btn dark" style="margin-top:14px">Write to me</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
